This looks like a CBP ruling on automotive A/C tubes/pipe assemblies. These are likely classified as parts of air conditioning machines under 8415.90, specifically 8415.90.80 (other parts), with the statistical suffix 8415.90.8045 or 8415.90.8065.

HTS 8415.90.80: "Parts: Other: Other." Statistical suffixes: 8415.90.8010 (evaporator/condenser for motor vehicles?), 8415.90.8045 (Other: Parts of air-conditioning machines of a kind used for persons in motor vehicles... ), 8415.90.8065 (Other). I recall that 8415.90.80 has 8415.90.8005 (Evaporators and condensers?), 8415.90.8045 (Other: Of a kind used in motor vehicles), 8415.90.8085 (Other). I will pick 8415.90.8045.

{"hts_code": "8415.90.8045", "reason": "Bent pipes and fittings made to connect components of a motor vehicle air conditioning system are parts of air conditioning machines, classified in heading 8415 as other parts for motor vehicle use."}
